# THE Core-#8 SWALLOW GUARD (error-model.md §11, Increment 2.1d — the reason the
# `bounds_panic` block on FaultScope exists). A callee raises Bounds, but the
# caller catches ONLY `Fault.Overflow:` → the Bounds tag is a category this scope
# does NOT catch. It must RE-PANIC "index out of bounds" (exit 1), NOT silently
# fall through to the result (which would be a silent miscompile). Without the
# always-Some bounds_handler → bounds_panic resolution, the deep Bounds would be
# swallowed.
int getx(Vector[int] xs, int i): xs[i]

void main():
    Vector[int] xs = [10, 20, 30]
    int r = getx(xs, 99) catch Fault.Overflow: 555   # Bounds NOT caught here → re-panic
    print(f"{r}")                                    # never reached
